  "body": "Promotes the existing non-normative note about focused-area preservation to normative prose, and explicitly states that no `focus` or `blur` events fire as a side effect of a `Document` moving into or out of the back/forward cache. This aligns the spec text with the implementer agreement reached in #5878 and matches WebKit's shipping behavior.\n\nCompanion issue: #12496 \n\nMotivating implementation: Chromium CL https://crrev.com/c/7829940 (https://crbug.com/40199280) is blocked on this clarification.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] At least two implementers are interested (and none opposed):\n  * WebKit: already implements this behavior.\n  * Chromium: implementing in https://crrev.com/c/7829940.\n  * Gecko: focus is preserved today; `blur`/`focus` event suppression part may need a follow-up.\n- [x] Tests are written and can be reviewed and commented upon at:\n  * https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/master/html/browsers/browsing-the-web/back-forward-cache/focus.html (existing, from web-platform-tests/wpt#31084).\n- [ ] Implementation bugs are filed:\n  * Chromium: https://crbug.com/40199280\n  * Gecko: (TBD)\n  * WebKit: n/a (already matches)\n- [ ] Corresponding HTML AAM & ARIA in HTML issues & PRs: n/a (no element semantics changed).\n- [ ] MDN issue is filed: (TBD)\n- [x] The top of this comment includes a clear commit message to use.\n\n```\nPreserve focused area across bfcache reactivation\n\nPromotes the existing note's preservation statement to normative prose\nand clarifies that no focus or blur events fire as a side effect of a\nDocument moving into or out of the back/forward cache. This aligns the\nspec text with the implementer agreement reached in #5878.\n```\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12497/interaction.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 27, 2026, 8:47 PM UTC (72a193f)\">/interaction.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/12497/e1f2525...72a193f/interaction.html\" title=\"Last updated on May 27, 2026, 8:47 PM UTC (72a193f)\">diff</a> )",
